# JavaScript / TypeScript Rules

## TypeScript
- Strict mode enabled (`strict: true` in tsconfig)
- Explicit return types on exported functions
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
- Use `unknown` over `any`; narrow types explicitly
- Prefer `const` over `let`; never use `var`

## React
- Functional components only (no class components)
- Custom hooks for reusable logic (prefix: `use`)
- Memoize expensive computations (`useMemo`, `useCallback`)
- Keys on list items (never index as key for dynamic lists)
- No `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` — use Zustand + DB persistence

## State Management
- Zustand for global state
- React Query / SWR for server state
- Local state (`useState`) only for UI-only state
- Never duplicate server state in client store

## API Calls
- Centralized API client (single `api.ts` module)
- Type-safe request/response interfaces
- Error handling in service layer, not components
- Loading/error states in UI for all async operations

## Styling
- Tailwind CSS utility classes
- shadcn/ui for component library
- No inline styles except dynamic values
- Responsive design (mobile-first)

## Security
- Never trust client-side validation alone
- Sanitize dynamic content before rendering
- CORS configuration matches allowed origins
- No secrets in frontend code (use backend proxy)
